// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
// specs/t27f/reel_topics.t27 -- the topics a reel can be made of, as data: the 27 lessons of
// course 0 (t27 basics) in English and Russian, each with its title, goal, task and spec code.
//
// WHY: the owner asked for a reel for every course and every lesson, made by the token_floor
// template, in two languages, by a generator rather than one reel at a time, and with the source
// in t27. specs/t27f/topic_reel_gen.t27 reads only this module; a topic is an index into it.
//
// WHAT IS HERE: tool-written data, not hand-typed. Text is stored as Unicode code points (u16)
// so the Russian survives an ASCII-only source: an item is TEXT_CP[ITEM_START[i] ..
// ITEM_START[i] + ITEM_LEN[i]]. The items, in order:
//   item(t, lang, f) = (t * 2 + lang) * 3 + f   lesson t, lang 0 en / 1 ru, f 0 title, 1 goal, 2 task
//   ID_ITEM0 + t                                lesson t's id, also its page t27.ai/learn/<id>/
//   COURSE_ITEM0 + lang * 2 + 0                 the course title
//   COURSE_ITEM0 + lang * 2 + 1                 "Lesson {0} of {1}", filled in by the generator
// Code is the lesson's spec with comment and blank lines dropped, ASCII bytes: line l is
// CODE[LINE_START[l] .. LINE_START[l + 1]], lesson t owns lines TOPIC_LINE0[t] .. TOPIC_LINE0[t + 1].
//
// PROVENANCE (2026-10-18; stock tools, no script):
//   gHashTag/trinity at SOURCE_COMMIT, SOURCE_FILE (generated there from the course's .t27 specs
//   and its Russian bundle); the COURSES array cut out with sed, then
//   jq '.[0] as $c | [($c.lessons[] | .en.title,.en.goal,.en.task,.ru.title,.ru.goal,.ru.task),
//       ($c.lessons[] | .id), $c.say.en.TITLE, $c.say.en.LESSON, $c.say.ru.TITLE,
//       $c.say.ru.LESSON] | map(explode)'                      -> TEXT_CP, ITEM_START, ITEM_LEN
//   each lesson's spec.source under apps/website/public, grep -v of comment and blank lines,
//   jq -R explode                                              -> CODE, LINE_START, TOPIC_LINE0
//
// The lessons, by index (jq to_entries of the en titles):
// 0 What a spec is, 1 The module line, 2 Comments and prose lines, 3 Constants, 4 Whole numbers
// and their widths, 5 True, false and text, 6 Arrays, 7 Trits: minus one, zero, one, 8
// Expressions, 9 A test block, 10 Many tests in one spec, 11 Functions, 12 Local names: let and
// var, 13 Choices: if, else and switch, 14 Loops: while and for, 15 pub or private, 16 Structs,
// 17 Enums, 18 Using other modules, 19 Invariants and benches, 20 gen-ts: a spec becomes
// TypeScript, 21 Seven backends, 22 The stages of t27c, 23 tri: the command line, 24 Reading
// compiler errors, 25 A small complete program, 26 Where to go next.
//
// NOT CLAIMED: only course 0 is here yet; the other eight courses and the blog posts take the same
// shape and come next. The text is the site's text at SOURCE_COMMIT, not re-edited for speech.
// phi^2 + 1/phi^2 = 3 | TRINITY

module reel_topics;

